  "explanation": "<strong>Step 1: Evaluate the first term</strong><br>$T_1 = \\Pi_X(\\sigma_{(P.Y = R.Y \\land R.V = V2)}(P \\times R))$<br><br>First, filter relation $R$ for tuples where $R.V = V2$:<br>- $(Y3, V2)$<br>- $(Y2, V2)$<br><br>Next, join these tuples with relation $P$ on $P.Y = R.Y$:<br>- For $R.Y = Y3$: No matching tuple in $P$.<br>- For $R.Y = Y2$: The matching tuple in $P$ is $(X2, Y2, Z2)$.<br><br>Projecting attribute $X$ gives:<br>$T_1 = \\{X2\\}$<br><br><strong>Step 2: Evaluate the second term</strong><br>$T_2 = \\Pi_X(\\sigma_{(Q.Y = R.Y \\land Q.T > 2)}(Q \\times R))$<br><br>First, filter relation $Q$ for tuples where $Q.T > 2$:<br>- $(X1, Y2, 5)$<br>- $(X1, Y1, 6)$<br><br>Next, check if $Q.Y$ exists in $R.Y$:<br>- For $(X1, Y2, 5)$: $Q.Y = Y2$, which exists in $R$.<br>- For $(X1, Y1, 6)$: $Q.Y = Y1$, which exists in $R$.<br><br>Projecting attribute $X$ gives:<br>$T_2 = \\{X1\\}$<br><br><strong>Step 3: Evaluate the set difference</strong><br>$T_1 - T_2 = \\{X2\\} - \\{X1\\} = \\{X2\\}$<br><br>The number of tuples returned is $1$.<br><br><strong>Correct Answer: 1</strong>",
